From b9f4b663093b6f2412b83adc0da05ff1a722d8ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:25:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] real_type option: numerical type of the generic interfaces

- MFront/GenericBehaviour/Types.h and MFront/GenericMaterialProperty/Types.h:
  mfront_gb_real and mfront_gmp_real are given by the MFRONT_GB_REAL_TYPE
  and MFRONT_GMP_REAL_TYPE macros if they are defined, double otherwise.
- new DSL option real_type (double by default, or float), written in the
  description and forwarded with the common options. With float, the
  generic and generic-parallel interfaces define both macros at the
  beginning of their generated headers and sources. The other interfaces
  and the models refuse it.
- each entry point of those interfaces exports the size in bytes of its
  numerical type (<f>_real_size, computed at compile time). The versions of
  their application programming interfaces (_api_version,
  _generic_parallel_api_version) are shifted by 1000 for a numerical type
  other than double, so that a caller expecting double refuses the
  library even if it does not read the size.
- generic-parallel: the ordered key of the time step scaling factor is
  built from its value converted to double, whatever the numerical type.
- ExternalLibraryManager::getRealSize reads the size (sizeof(double) if the
  symbol is not defined, for older libraries); MTest refuses a generic
  behaviour whose numerical type is not double.
